{"name":"Wicked Witch","hex":"#5b984f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wicked","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Evil or mischievous by nature; morally reprehensible.","Harsh; severe."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To a superlative extent, very, extremely"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wicked"},{"term":"witch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person (now usually particularly a woman) who uses magical or supernatural powers to influence or predict events, particularly one with malicious motives.\n\n A person of any gender who harmfully employs magical power (especially innate rather than ritual)","A person of any gender who harmfully employs magical power (especially innate rather than ritual)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dowse for water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wicked Witch of the West","blocks":[{"text":"The Wicked Witch of the West is a character in the classic children's novel The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900) by the American author L. Frank Baum, who is the evil ruler of the Winkie Country, the western region in the Land of Oz. She is inadvertently killed by the child Dorothy Gale with a bucket of water. In Baum's subsequent Oz novels, the Wicked Witch of the West is referred to occasionally."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicked_Witch_of_the_West","wikidata":"Q3822980"},{"title":"Wicked (Maguire novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Wicked: The Life and Times of the Wicked Witch of the West is a 1995 dark fantasy novel by American writer Gregory Maguire, with illustrations by Douglas Smith. It is the first novel in The Wicked Years series, and was followed by Son of a Witch, A Lion Among Men, and Out of Oz, plus a number of short stories since 2012."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/70/WickedBookCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicked_(Maguire_novel)","wikidata":"Q1735754"},{"title":"Witchcraft","blocks":[{"text":"Witchcraft is the use of magic by a person called a witch. Traditionally, \"witchcraft\" means the use of magic to inflict supernatural harm or misfortune on others, and this remains the most common and widespread meaning. Though the idea of witchcraft is largely imaginary, it has nevertheless served in many cultures as a way to explain the presence of evil. The belief in witches has been found throughout history in a great number of societies worldwide. Most of these societies have used protective magic or counter-magic against witchcraft, and have shunned, banished, imprisoned, physically punished or killed alleged witches. Anthropologists use the term \"witchcraft\" for similar beliefs about harmful occult practices in different cultures, and these societies often use the term when speaking in English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG/330px-John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witchcraft","wikidata":"Q259745"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Wicked_Witch_of_the_West.png/500px-Wicked_Witch_of_the_West.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Wicked_Witch_of_the_West.png/500px-Wicked_Witch_of_the_West.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWicked_Witch_of_the_West.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/The_Wizard_of_Oz_Margaret_Hamilton_Judy_Garland_1939.jpg/330px-The_Wizard_of_Oz_Margaret_Hamilton_Judy_Garland_1939.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h